<title>GERMANY: Rexrodt urges focus on competitive steel jobs.</title>
<headline>Rexrodt urges focus on competitive steel jobs.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Economics Minister Guenter Rexrodt, saying he neither favoured nor objected to Krupp's planned takeover of rival Thyssen AG, on Tuesday said the focus must be on retaining competitive jobs in the steel sector.</p>
<p>&quot;The goal cannot be to eliminate jobs,&quot; he said. &quot;At the forefront must be the survival of the German steel industry.&quot;</p>
<p>Earlier Fried. Krupp AG Hoesch-Krupp confirmed that it planned to make a bid for its larger rival Thyssen and said it was &quot;fairly confident&quot; the bid would succeed.</p>
<p>Thyssen has vowed to fend off the attack.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49 228 26097 150</p>
</text>
